  "design": {
    "proof": "A module-private WeakMap records only the factory-created chunk and its factory-created ordinary reference object. It records origin, not validated values.",
    "ordinaryProducer": "The existing DictionaryDatabase producer retains one object spread, ordinary own fields, prepared-index handling and fresh resolved-reference object shape. It now records that object origin via the factory.",
    "genericBehavior": "Unmarked chunks, Proxy wrappers, replaced reference objects, accessor-backed references and columns, shared columns and subclasses use the original per-row validation path. Prototype/descriptor checks are not used as a proof that an arbitrary caller object is not a Proxy.",
    "awaitBoundaries": "Each run rechecks the current own reference descriptor, exact original reference-object identity, prototypes and current column descriptors/types/bounds. Offset and length values are validated again after every awaited append; no validity is cached.",
    "optimization": "The existing consecutive-ID run loop is unchanged for eligible producer objects. Exact encoder outputs match generic output; a120-row consecutive-alias test observes one offset validation versus120 generic validations.",
    "typedKindSpoofTriage": "No unrelated typed-kind guards were added. Actual-encoder tests show spoofed typed-array prototypes with an invalid first offset/length still throw before append."
